WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.160
We've reached Full Circle.

2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.800
Look back at page four, at the young
person you described

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.040
and the one thing you wanted to know.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.920
What feels clearer now?

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.240
What question remains?

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.200
Take a moment privately, or share a brief
reflection

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.040
if you wish.

8
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.640
Then look again at the strengths and joys
you wrote down.

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.160
Pause here before we choose what to carry
forward.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.440
Keep that whole person in view.

11
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.090
We're going to finish with a few small
actions that connect home,

12
00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.440
school and positive identity.

13
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.350
You don't need a long list, and you don't
need to have answered every

14
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.080
question today.

15
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.080
Belonging, capacity and joy give us three
connected questions to return

16
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:55.680
to.

17
00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.180
Can your young person be recognised,
included and able to participate

18
00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.680
as themselves?

19
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.680
What does the day cost,

20
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.680
and what protects or restores energy?

21
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.680
Where are the interests, connections and
moments of authentic enjoyment?

22
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.680
When you try a change at home or school,
look across all three.

23
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.680
Getting through a task is only part of the
picture.

24
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.680
The effect on energy and belonging matters
too.

25
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.970
Your young person's own response will help
you judge whether a change

26
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:26.680
is useful.

27
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.600
Turn to Three small things on page
eighteen.

28
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.480
First, one thing to try at home this week.

29
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.260
Keep it small enough to begin.

30
00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.760
Second, one thing you would like school to
know, understand or support,

31
00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.980
and the sentence you will open with.

32
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.460
Your notes from page seventeen can help.

33
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.080
Third, one strength you see in your young
person,

34
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.300
and a plan to tell them this week.

35
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.500
Look back at page four if you need a
starting point.

36
00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.120
You might name the strength privately, in
a message or in another way

37
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.760
that suits your young person.

38
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.710
If this is a difficult time and one
strength is all you can manage

39
00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.460
today, that is enough.

40
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.400
Pause the recording while you write.

41
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.120
Read your notes once more.

42
00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.160
Are they manageable in your real week?

43
00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.720
You can make a step smaller,

44
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.680
leave something for later or ask for help.

45
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.440
Keep the page somewhere you'll see it
again.

46
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.120
The plan can change as you learn what
helps.

47
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.950
Connection can continue through other
families, local or online parent

48
00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.060
groups, and opportunities to learn
together.

49
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.620
If you're with others today, you can
exchange contact details if

50
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.800
everyone wishes.

51
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.140
Choose what fits you.

52
00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.660
The supplied materials still list webinar
titles and dates as to be

53
00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.300
confirmed, and the Community of Practice
link as to be added.

54
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.400
We can't give confirmed access details for
those yet.

55
00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.710
Check current arrangements with the
workshop team or Positive

56
00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.520
Partnerships.

57
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.750
Asking for support is part of parenting,
and there is room to keep

58
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.520
learning after today.

59
00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.300
It can also show your young person that
asking for help is welcome.

60
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.900
The Positive Partnerships website has
resources for families on many of

61
00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.640
the topics we've explored.

62
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.440
The address is positive partnerships dot
com dot A U.

63
00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.840
The slide also shows the organisation's
social media channels.

64
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.840
Pause if you would like to note or
photograph those details.

65
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.840
Your workbook has a resource list you can
return to later.

66
00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.120
Feedback helps the team understand what
was useful and what could be

67
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.000
clearer.

68
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.970
This source slide still has a placeholder
for the feedback link and Q R

69
00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:53.320
code,

70
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.400
so there is no active form to open here.

71
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.960
For now, you can write down one useful
idea, one remaining question

72
00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.840
and anything that would make participation
easier.

73
00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.240
Keep those notes to share through the
confirmed feedback arrangements

74
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.200
when they are available.

75
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.600
Pause here if you would like time.

76
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Keep your feedback with your workbook.

77
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.740
Your experience can help shape how the
workshop is delivered for other

78
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.000
families.

79
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.620
Thank you for making time for this
learning and for the care you bring

80
00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.480
to understanding your young person.

81
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.360
Keep your workbook and the small steps
you've chosen.

82
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.310
Stay curious, keep your young person at
the centre, and include the

83
00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:40.800
people who know them well.

84
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.480
Try one manageable change,

85
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.860
notice what happens and adjust as you go.

86
00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:50.140
There is room for a good day, a difficult
day and a fresh question.

87
00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.610
The young person you brought to mind at
the beginning remains the

88
00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.920
person we come back to:

89
00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.300
someone with strengths, interests and a
life worth understanding.
